+++ b/packaging/UPSTREAM_SOURCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
+# Pinned upstream source archives
+
+`upstream_source.py` is the archive validation primitive for plugins maintained
+in another repository. It does not register a plugin, stage installed files,
+execute downloaded code, download assets, or authorize signing or publication.
+Existing `plugins.json` records and publication admission are unchanged.
+
+A reviewed JSON lock contains exactly seven string fields:
+
+| Field | Required value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `repository` | GitHub owner/repository |
+| `tag` | Versioned release tag, such as `v1.2.3` |
+| `commit` | Full lowercase 40-character source revision |
+| `url` | HTTPS `github.com/OWNER/REPO/releases/download/TAG/ASSET.tar.gz` |
+| `sha256` | Lowercase SHA256 of the compressed archive |
+| `root` | Single root directory in that archive |
+| `plugin` | Relative plugin subtree under the archive root |
+
+The lock author must independently review the release tag's source revision and
+asset provenance. An archive digest binds its bytes; it does not independently
+prove the publisher's tag/commit assertion. Do not create a release lock from a
+mutable branch, an unreviewed asset, or an unsigned development package.
+
+With a locally cached archive and a reviewed lock:
+
+```sh
+python3 packaging/upstream_source.py --archive /path/to/source.tar.gz --lock /path/to/source.json
+```
+
+The command verifies the compressed digest before parsing, bounds compressed
+bytes, decompression, member count and expanded file bytes, and reports the
+complete source file inventory and per-file SHA256. It rejects duplicate paths,
+noncanonical paths, root escapes, links, sparse files, devices, privileged modes,
+file/directory collisions and a missing plugin subtree. It never extracts files
+onto the host. A private temporary spool bounds decompression before tar headers
+are parsed and is closed on both success and failure.
+
+`nethub_source.py` provides the NetHub-specific copied-file reconstruction. It
+reads the verified inventory, reproduces the builder's source-copy exclusions,
+returns all four exact lifecycle hooks, checks the package/product version and
+identity, and fingerprints ten compiler, module, builder and license-collector
+inputs. It refuses copied files outside `/usr/local` or in the generated binary
+directory. It does not execute upstream scripts or compile a client.
+
+## Comparing a candidate package
+
+`nethub_package.py` compares a candidate with the reconstructed source and a
+separately reviewed build record. It reuses the publication verifier's existing
+file-inventory and lifecycle-hook comparisons. Extracting those comparisons into
+shared functions does not change the checks for existing registered plugins.
+
+The build record is a JSON object with exactly these fields:
+
+| Field | Required value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `schema_version` | Integer `1` |
+| `source_commit`, `source_archive_sha256` | Exact source-lock values |
+| `abi` | Reviewed native `FreeBSD:MAJOR:amd64` target |
+| `compiler`, `frp_version` | Source compiler/frp pins |
+| `build_input_sha256` | All ten fingerprints returned by the source adapter |
+| `generated_files` | Complete relative generated-file paths mapped to SHA256 |
+
+The generated-file directory contains the independent reviewed build outputs,
+relative to `/usr/local/opnsense/nethub-agent/bin/`. It must include `frpc`,
+`FRP_BUILD.json`, `FRP_VERSION`, `FRP_LICENSE` and the complete `frpc-licenses/`
+tree. The Go license and the versioned upstream frp license are mandatory.
+The collector's canonical `frpc-licenses/modules.txt` must cover exactly the
+module license directories, each containing a collected license or notice.
+The record itself also requires a separately reviewed SHA256 supplied explicitly
+to the command. Create and review these pins from an independent accepted build;
+**deriving the record or cache from the candidate under test is not acceptance**.
+
+```sh
+python3 packaging/nethub_package.py \
+  --package /path/to/candidate.pkg \
+  --archive /path/to/source.tar.gz \
+  --source-lock /path/to/source.json \
+  --build-record /path/to/reviewed-build.json \
+  --build-record-sha256 "$REVIEWED_BUILD_RECORD_SHA256" \
+  --generated-directory /path/to/independent-generated-files
+```
+
+The command binds the generated bytes to their complete inventory, source inputs,
+compiler, module locks and frpc profile. It checks the FreeBSD ELF target, receipt,
+version and corresponding license bytes without executing the binary. It then
+compares candidate metadata, ABI, dependencies, flat size, file ownership/modes,
+complete copied/generated contents and all four hooks. The package and catalog
+manifests must agree, and unreviewed manifest fields or per-file attributes are
+rejected. Both archive readers used by the existing verifier remain required.
+All candidate readers and the reported package digest use one bounded private
+snapshot. The reported digest identifies those verified bytes, not a mutable
+filename; the release process must match the actual package's digest before
+signing or publishing it.
+
+Success proves candidate-byte agreement with the supplied reviewed inputs. It
+does not independently prove the reviewer's build provenance, native behavior,
+the completeness of the reviewer's dependency-license collection, or release
+approval. The command explicitly reports native lifecycle/release acceptance as
+false. No NetHub release record or placeholder release pins are installed here.
+Connecting this support to the publication registry, independently reviewing real
+release inputs, native lifecycle validation and owner approval remain required
+before signing or publication.
+
+Validation: `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_upstream_source.py -v`.
+The adapter and candidate tests use `test_nethub_source.py` and
+`test_nethub_package.py` with the same command. The existing shared-suite discovery
+includes all three suites. Synthetic source archives, ELF headers and packages
+in these tests are fixtures, not release records or native build acceptance.
diff --git a/packaging/nethub_package.py b/packaging/nethub_package.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cb4863f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packaging/nethub_package.py
@@ -0,0 +1,224 @@
+"""Compare a NetHub candidate package with pinned source and reviewed build bytes."""
+import argparse
+import hashlib
+import importlib.util
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+import stat
+import struct
+import tempfile
+
+
+def load_module(name, path):
+    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path)
+    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
+    spec.loader.exec_module(module)
+    return module
+
+
+HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+source = load_module('nethub_package_source', HERE / 'nethub_source.py')
+verify = load_module('nethub_package_verifier', HERE.parent / 'verify-repo.py')
+MAX_FILE_BYTES = 64 * 1024 * 1024
+MAX_BUILD_BYTES = 128 * 1024 * 1024
+MAX_PACKAGE_BYTES = 256 * 1024 * 1024
+RECORD_FIELDS = {'schema_version', 'source_commit', 'source_archive_sha256', 'abi',
+                 'compiler', 'frp_version', 'build_input_sha256', 'generated_files'}
+REQUIRED_OUTPUTS = {'frpc', 'FRP_BUILD.json', 'FRP_VERSION', 'FRP_LICENSE',
+                    'frpc-licenses/GO-LICENSE', 'frpc-licenses/modules.txt'}
+EXECUTABLE_SOURCE = {'/usr/local/etc/rc.d/nethub_agent_frpc',
+    '/usr/local/etc/rc.syshook.d/early/14-nethub-agent-trust',
+    '/usr/local/etc/rc.syshook.d/early/15-nethub-agent-certificate',
+    '/usr/local/etc/rc.syshook.d/start/20-nethub-agent'}
+
+
+def digest(raw):
+    return hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()
+
+
+def read_pinned_record(path, sha256):
+    if not isinstance(sha256, str) or not re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', sha256):
+        raise ValueError('A reviewed build-record SHA256 is required.')
+    path = Path(path)
+    if path.is_symlink() or not path.is_file():
+        raise ValueError('Build record must be a regular file.')
+    with path.open('rb') as stream:
+        raw = stream.read(2 * 1024 * 1024 + 1)
+    if len(raw) > 2 * 1024 * 1024 or digest(raw) != sha256:
+        raise ValueError('Build record differs from its reviewed digest.')
+    record = source.json_object(raw)
+    if set(record) != RECORD_FIELDS or type(record['schema_version']) is not int or record['schema_version'] != 1:
+        raise ValueError('Build record has an unsupported schema.')
+    return record
+
+
+def generated_files(directory, record, stage, lock):
+    for key, expected in [('source_commit', lock['commit']), ('source_archive_sha256', lock['sha256']),
+                          ('compiler', stage['compiler']), ('frp_version', stage['frp_version']),
+                          ('build_input_sha256', stage['build_input_sha256'])]:
+        if record[key] != expected:
+            raise ValueError('Build record differs from pinned source inputs: ' + key)
+    if not isinstance(record['abi'], str) or not re.fullmatch(verify.ABI_PATTERN, record['abi']):
+        raise ValueError('Build record must pin a native FreeBSD amd64 ABI.')
+    declared = record['generated_files']
+    if not isinstance(declared, dict) or not REQUIRED_OUTPUTS <= set(declared) or len(declared) > 20000:
+        raise ValueError('Build record lacks a complete generated-file inventory.')
+    upstream_license = 'frpc-licenses/github.com/fatedier/frp@v' + stage['frp_version'] + '/LICENSE'
+    if upstream_license not in declared:
+        raise ValueError('Build record lacks the upstream frp license.')
+    for name, expected in declared.items():
+        source.upstream.relative_path(name)
+        if name not in REQUIRED_OUTPUTS and not name.startswith('frpc-licenses/'):
+            raise ValueError('Build record contains an unexpected generated output.')
+        if not isinstance(expected, str) or not re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', expected):
+            raise ValueError('Build record contains an invalid generated-file digest.')
+    root = Path(directory)
+    if root.is_symlink() or not root.is_dir():
+        raise ValueError('Generated-file cache must be a regular directory.')
+    actual = {}
+    total = 0
+    for path in root.rglob('*'):
+        mode = path.lstat().st_mode
+        if stat.S_ISLNK(mode) or not (stat.S_ISDIR(mode) or stat.S_ISREG(mode)):
+            raise ValueError('Generated-file cache contains a link or special entry.')
+        if stat.S_ISDIR(mode):
+            continue
+        name = path.relative_to(root).as_posix()
+        if name not in declared or path.stat().st_nlink != 1:
+            raise ValueError('Generated-file cache differs from its closed inventory.')
+        with path.open('rb') as stream:
+            raw = stream.read(MAX_FILE_BYTES + 1)
+        total += len(raw)
+        if len(raw) > MAX_FILE_BYTES or total > MAX_BUILD_BYTES:
+            raise ValueError('Generated-file cache exceeds its size bound.')
+        if digest(raw) != declared[name]:
+            raise ValueError('Generated-file cache differs from reviewed bytes: ' + name)
+        actual[name] = raw
+    if set(actual) != set(declared):
+        raise ValueError('Generated-file cache is missing a reviewed output.')
+    binary = actual['frpc']
+    if (len(binary) < 20 or binary[:8] != b'\x7fELF\x02\x01\x01\x09'
+            or struct.unpack('<HH', binary[16:20]) not in [(2, 62), (3, 62)]):
+        raise ValueError('Reviewed frpc is not a FreeBSD amd64 ELF executable.')
+    receipt = source.json_object(actual['FRP_BUILD.json'])
+    expected_receipt = {'compiler': stage['compiler'], 'frp_version': stage['frp_version'],
+        'target': 'freebsd_amd64', 'tags': ['frpc', 'noweb'],
+        'dependency_locks': {name: stage['build_input_sha256'][source.PLUGIN + '/frpc-build/' + name]
+                             for name in ['go.mod', 'go.sum']}, 'binary_sha256': digest(binary)}
+    if receipt != expected_receipt or actual['FRP_VERSION'] != (stage['frp_version'] + '\n').encode():
+        raise ValueError('Generated frpc receipt differs from source compiler/module/profile pins.')
+    if actual['FRP_LICENSE'] != actual[upstream_license] or not actual['FRP_LICENSE'].strip() or not actual['frpc-licenses/GO-LICENSE'].strip():
+        raise ValueError('Generated license inventory disagrees with the installed licenses.')
+    try:
+        modules = actual['frpc-licenses/modules.txt'].decode('ascii').splitlines()
+    except UnicodeError as error:
+        raise ValueError('Generated module license index is not canonical ASCII.') from error
+    if (not modules or modules != sorted(set(modules))
+            or actual['frpc-licenses/modules.txt'] != ('\n'.join(modules) + '\n').encode('ascii')
+            or 'github.com/fatedier/frp@v' + stage['frp_version'] not in modules):
+        raise ValueError('Generated module license index is incomplete or noncanonical.')
+    for name in modules:
+        source.upstream.relative_path(name)
+        if '@v' not in name or not any(path.startswith('frpc-licenses/' + name + '/') for path in actual):
+            raise ValueError('Generated module license index names an uncovered module.')
+    for path in actual:
+        if not path.startswith('frpc-licenses/') or path in REQUIRED_OUTPUTS:
+            continue
+        matches = [name for name in modules if path.startswith('frpc-licenses/' + name + '/')]
+        if len(matches) != 1:
+            raise ValueError('Generated license file is outside the module index.')
+        relative = path[len('frpc-licenses/' + matches[0] + '/'):]
+        if not relative.split('/')[0].lower().startswith(('license', 'licence', 'copying', 'notice', 'copyright')):
+            raise ValueError('Generated module file is not a collected license or notice.')
+    return {source.GENERATED + name: raw for name, raw in actual.items()}
+
+
+def verify_snapshot(package, archive, lock, build_record, build_record_sha256, generated_directory):
+    """Use one private package snapshot for all readers and the returned digest."""
+    record = read_pinned_record(build_record, build_record_sha256)
+    stage = source.reconstruct(archive, lock)
+    outputs = generated_files(generated_directory, record, stage, lock)
+    expected = dict(stage['files'])
+    if set(expected) & set(outputs):
+        raise ValueError('Generated outputs replace copied source files.')
+    expected.update(outputs)
+    package = Path(package)
+    manifest = verify.manifest_of(package)
+    verify.check_manifest_shape(package, manifest)
+    substitutions = {'VERSION': stage['version'], 'ABI': record['abi'],
+                     'ARCH': 'freebsd:' + record['abi'].split(':')[1] + ':x86:64'}
+    text = json.dumps(stage['manifest_template'])
+    for name, value in substitutions.items():
+        text = text.replace('@' + name + '@', value)
+    metadata = json.loads(text)
+    metadata['desc'] = stage['description']
+    if any(manifest.get(name) != value for name, value in metadata.items()):
+        raise ValueError('Candidate package metadata differs from pinned source and ABI.')
+    if set(manifest) - (set(metadata) | {'files', 'scripts', 'flatsize', 'deps'}):
+        raise ValueError('Candidate package contains unreviewed manifest fields.')
+    if not isinstance(manifest.get('deps', {}), dict) or manifest.get('deps', {}) != metadata.get('deps', {}):
+        raise ValueError('Candidate package dependencies differ from pinned source.')
+    if type(manifest.get('flatsize')) is not int or manifest['flatsize'] != sum(map(len, expected.values())):
+        raise ValueError('Candidate package flat size differs from reconstructed files.')
+    if not isinstance(manifest.get('files'), dict) or not isinstance(manifest.get('scripts'), dict):
+        raise ValueError('Candidate package has no complete file and hook inventories.')
+    if any(not isinstance(value, str) for value in manifest['scripts'].values()):
+        raise ValueError('Candidate lifecycle hooks must be strings.')
+    if any(not isinstance(value, str) for value in manifest['files'].values()):
+        raise ValueError('Candidate package carries unreviewed per-file manifest attributes.')
+    for member in verify.python_members(package):
+        if not member.isfile():
+            raise ValueError('NetHub candidate package must contain only regular files.')
+        name = '/' + member.name.removeprefix('./').lstrip('/')
+        executable = name in EXECUTABLE_SOURCE or name == source.GENERATED + 'frpc'
+        if member.mode != (0o755 if executable else 0o644) or member.uid != 0 or member.gid != 0:
+            raise ValueError('Candidate file permissions or ownership differ from the builder: ' + name)
+    verify.verify_file_inventory(package, manifest, expected)
+    verify.verify_lifecycle_hooks(manifest, stage['scripts'])
+    with package.open('rb') as stream:
+        package_sha256 = hashlib.file_digest(stream, 'sha256').hexdigest()
+    return {'source_commit': lock['commit'], 'source_archive_sha256': lock['sha256'],
+            'build_record_sha256': build_record_sha256, 'package_sha256': package_sha256,
+            'files_compared': len(expected), 'hooks_compared': len(stage['scripts']),
+            'matches_reviewed_inputs_and_bytes': True, 'native_lifecycle_or_release_accepted': False}
+
+
+def verify_candidate(package, archive, lock, build_record, build_record_sha256, generated_directory):
+    """Verify candidate bytes only; this does not authorize signing or publication.
+
+    The build-record digest is a separate review input. Deriving that record from
+    the candidate under test would destroy its independence and is not acceptance.
+    A native build/lifecycle report and the owner's release approval remain gates.
+    """
+    original = Path(package)
+    if original.is_symlink() or not original.is_file():
+        raise ValueError('Candidate package must be a regular file.')
+    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='nethub-candidate-') as temporary:
+        snapshot = Path(temporary) / 'candidate.pkg'
+        total = 0
+        with original.open('rb') as stream, snapshot.open('xb') as output:
+            while block := stream.read(65536):
+                total += len(block)
+                if total > MAX_PACKAGE_BYTES:
+                    raise ValueError('Candidate package exceeds its size bound.')
+                output.write(block)
+        return verify_snapshot(snapshot, archive, lock, build_record, build_record_sha256, generated_directory)
+
+
+def main():
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
+    parser.add_argument('--package', type=Path, required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--archive', type=Path, required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--source-lock', type=Path, required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--build-record', type=Path, required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--build-record-sha256', required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--generated-directory', type=Path, required=True)
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+    result = verify_candidate(args.package, args.archive, source.upstream.load_lock(args.source_lock),
+                              args.build_record, args.build_record_sha256, args.generated_directory)
+    print(json.dumps(result, sort_keys=True))
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    main()
diff --git a/packaging/nethub_source.py b/packaging/nethub_source.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..42d21c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packaging/nethub_source.py
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+"""Reconstruct NetHub's copied package files and hooks from a pinned archive."""
+import hashlib
+import importlib.util
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+
+
+SPEC = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(
+    'repository_upstream_source', Path(__file__).with_name('upstream_source.py'))
+upstream = importlib.util.module_from_spec(SPEC)
+SPEC.loader.exec_module(upstream)
+
+PLUGIN = 'agents/opnsense/plugin'
+PRODUCT_PATH = '/usr/local/opnsense/version/nethub-agent'
+GENERATED = '/usr/local/opnsense/nethub-agent/bin/'
+HOOKS = {'pre-install': '+PRE_INSTALL', 'post-install': '+POST_INSTALL',
+         'pre-deinstall': '+PRE_DEINSTALL', 'post-deinstall': '+POST_DEINSTALL'}
+BUILD_INPUTS = [PLUGIN + '/' + name for name in (
+    'build.sh', 'build.py', 'frpc_source.py', 'frp_artifact.py', 'frp-artifacts.json',
+    'FRP_VERSION', 'frpc-build/go.mod', 'frpc-build/go.sum')]
+BUILD_INPUTS += ['server/.go-version', 'deploy/images/licenses.go']
+
+
+def json_object(raw):
+    def unique(pairs):
+        result = {}
+        for name, value in pairs:
+            if name in result:
+                raise ValueError('NetHub metadata contains duplicate keys.')
+            result[name] = value
+        return result
+
+    value = json.loads(raw, object_pairs_hook=unique)
+    if not isinstance(value, dict):
+        raise ValueError('NetHub metadata must be a JSON object.')
+    return value
+
+
+def reconstruct(archive, lock):
+    """Describe copied source only; generated frpc bytes still need verification.
+
+    This does not run the upstream builder, register a publishing record or
+    claim that a compiled executable matches the source. The caller must compare
+    the returned inventory and hooks with a candidate package and independently
+    bind all generated files to the reviewed build-input fingerprints.
+    """
+    upstream.validate_lock(lock)
+    if lock['repository'] != 'KazuhaHub/nethub' or lock['plugin'] != PLUGIN:
+        raise ValueError('This source adapter requires the NetHub plugin subtree.')
+    source = upstream.read_source(archive, lock)
+    prefix = PLUGIN + '/src/'
+    files = {}
+    for name, content in source.items():
+        if not name.startswith(prefix):
+            continue
+        relative = name[len(prefix):]
+        parts = relative.split('/')
+        # Match build.py's copytree ignore patterns, without executing it.
+        if any(part in {'.DS_Store', '__pycache__'} or part.startswith('._') for part in parts):
+            continue
+        destination = '/' + relative
+        if not destination.startswith('/usr/local/'):
+            raise ValueError('NetHub copied source leaves its installation prefix.')
+        if destination == GENERATED.rstrip('/') or destination.startswith(GENERATED):
+            raise ValueError('Copied source collides with NetHub generated build outputs.')
+        files[destination] = content
+    if PRODUCT_PATH not in files:
+        raise ValueError('NetHub source has no product version metadata.')
+    product = json_object(files[PRODUCT_PATH])
+    manifest_path = PLUGIN + '/packaging/freebsd/+MANIFEST.in'
+    try:
+        manifest = json_object(source[manifest_path])
+        description = source[PLUGIN + '/packaging/freebsd/pkg-descr'].decode('utf-8').strip()
+        scripts = {phase: source[PLUGIN + '/packaging/freebsd/' + name].decode('utf-8')
+                   for phase, name in HOOKS.items()}
+        build_inputs = {name: hashlib.sha256(source[name]).hexdigest() for name in BUILD_INPUTS}
+        versions = re.findall(rb'^VERSION=([^\s]+)$', source[PLUGIN + '/build.sh'], re.M)
+        compiler = source['server/.go-version'].decode('ascii').strip()
+        frp = json_object(source[PLUGIN + '/frp-artifacts.json'])
+        frp_version = source[PLUGIN + '/FRP_VERSION'].decode('ascii').strip()
+    except (KeyError, UnicodeError) as error:
+        raise ValueError('NetHub archive lacks complete package metadata or build inputs.') from error
+    if len(versions) != 1 or not re.fullmatch(rb'[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+', versions[0]):
+        raise ValueError('NetHub source declares no unambiguous package version.')
+    version = versions[0].decode('ascii')
+    if (product.get('product_id') != 'os-nethub-agent' or manifest.get('name') != 'os-nethub-agent'
+            or product.get('product_version') != version or manifest.get('version') != '@VERSION@'
+            or manifest.get('abi') != '@ABI@' or manifest.get('arch') != '@ARCH@'
+            or not isinstance(product.get('product_email'), str) or not product['product_email']
+            or product.get('product_email') != manifest.get('maintainer')
+            or product.get('product_website') != 'https://github.com/KazuhaHub/nethub'
+            or product.get('product_website') != manifest.get('www')
+            or manifest.get('licenses') != ['Apache-2.0']):
+        raise ValueError('NetHub package metadata disagrees with its source identity.')
+    if not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+', compiler) or frp.get('version') != frp_version:
+        raise ValueError('NetHub compiler or frp version locks disagree.')
+    if not description or any(not script.strip() for script in scripts.values()):
+        raise ValueError('NetHub package description or lifecycle hook is empty.')
+    return {'files': files, 'scripts': scripts, 'manifest_template': manifest,
+            'description': description, 'version': version, 'compiler': 'go' + compiler,
+            'frp_version': frp_version, 'build_input_sha256': build_inputs,
+            'generated_files_verified': False}
diff --git a/packaging/upstream_source.py b/packaging/upstream_source.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..64b6b8d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packaging/upstream_source.py
@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+"""Read a reviewed upstream release archive without executing or extracting it."""
+import argparse
+from contextlib import contextmanager
+import gzip
+import hashlib
+import io
+import json
+from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath
+import re
+import tarfile
+import tempfile
+
+
+MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES = 64 * 1024 * 1024
+MAX_SOURCE_BYTES = 256 * 1024 * 1024
+MAX_MEMBERS = 20000
+MAX_TAR_BYTES = MAX_SOURCE_BYTES + MAX_MEMBERS * 2048
+LOCK_FIELDS = {'repository', 'tag', 'commit', 'url', 'sha256', 'root', 'plugin'}
+
+
+def relative_path(value):
+    """Keep tar names canonical on both the build host and verification host."""
+    if (not isinstance(value, str) or not value or len(value) > 1024 or not value.isascii()
+            or re.search(r'[\x00-\x20\x7f\\:]', value)
+            or value.startswith('/') or PurePosixPath(value).as_posix() != value
+            or any(part in {'', '.', '..'} or len(part) > 255 for part in value.split('/'))):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream source path is not canonical.')
+    return value
+
+
+def validate_lock(lock):
+    """A digest is required even when the release URL contains a version tag."""
+    if not isinstance(lock, dict) or set(lock) != LOCK_FIELDS:
+        raise ValueError('Upstream source lock has unexpected fields.')
+    if not all(isinstance(value, str) for value in lock.values()):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream source lock values must be strings.')
+    if not re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+', lock['repository']):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream repository must be an owner/name pair.')
+    if not re.fullmatch(r'v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+(?:-[0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?', lock['tag']):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream source requires a versioned release tag.')
+    if not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{40}', lock['commit']):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream source requires a full commit pin.')
+    if not re.fullmatch(r'[0-9a-f]{64}', lock['sha256']):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream source requires an archive SHA256 pin.')
+    prefix = 'https://github.com/' + lock['repository'] + '/releases/download/' + lock['tag'] + '/'
+    if not lock['url'].startswith(prefix) or not re.fullmatch(
+            r'[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*\.tar\.gz', lock['url'][len(prefix):]):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream URL must name a release tar.gz asset.')
+    if '/' in relative_path(lock['root']):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream archive must have one pinned root directory.')
+    relative_path(lock['plugin'])
+    return lock
+
+
+def load_lock(path):
+    """Do not let duplicate JSON keys silently replace a reviewed pin."""
+    def unique(pairs):
+        value = {}
+        for name, item in pairs:
+            if name in value:
+                raise ValueError('Upstream source lock contains a duplicate key.')
+            value[name] = item
+        return value
+
+    return validate_lock(json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding='utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique))
+
+
+@contextmanager
+def tar_stream(raw):
+    """Bound decompression before tarfile can consume oversized PAX headers."""
+    with tempfile.SpooledTemporaryFile(max_size=1024 * 1024) as plain:
+        with gzip.GzipFile(fileobj=io.BytesIO(raw)) as compressed:
+            total = 0
+            while True:
+                block = compressed.read(min(65536, MAX_TAR_BYTES - total + 1))
+                if not block:
+                    break
+                total += len(block)
+                if total > MAX_TAR_BYTES:
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream archive exceeds the tar size limit.')
+                plain.write(block)
+        plain.seek(0)
+        with tarfile.open(fileobj=plain, mode='r:') as source:
+            yield source
+
+
+def read_source(archive, lock):
+    """Return the complete digest-bound file inventory; never trust a tar extractor.
+
+    The caller supplies a cached archive. This function does not download assets,
+    run upstream build scripts, or authorize publishing a package. The tag/commit
+    relationship must be reviewed when the lock is created; a digest binds bytes,
+    not the publisher's assertion that a tag names a particular commit.
+    """
+    validate_lock(lock)
+    archive = Path(archive)
+    if archive.is_symlink() or not archive.is_file():
+        raise ValueError('Upstream archive must be a regular cached file.')
+    with archive.open('rb') as stream:
+        raw = stream.read(MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES + 1)
+    if len(raw) > MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES:
+        raise ValueError('Upstream archive exceeds the compressed size limit.')
+    if hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest() != lock['sha256']:
+        raise ValueError('Upstream archive differs from its SHA256 pin.')
+    files, seen = {}, set()
+    expanded = 0
+    try:
+        with tar_stream(raw) as source:
+            for index, member in enumerate(source):
+                if index >= MAX_MEMBERS:
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream archive exceeds the member limit.')
+                name = member.name
+                if member.isdir() and name.endswith('/'):
+                    name = name[:-1]
+                relative_path(name)
+                if name in seen:
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream archive contains a duplicate path.')
+                seen.add(name)
+                if name != lock['root'] and not name.startswith(lock['root'] + '/'):
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream archive leaves its pinned root.')
+                if member.mode & 0o7000:
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream archive contains privileged file modes.')
+                if name == lock['root']:
+                    if not member.isdir():
+                        raise ValueError('Upstream archive root must be a directory.')
+                    continue
+                if (not member.isfile() and not member.isdir()) or member.issparse():
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream archive contains a link or special entry.')
+                if member.isdir():
+                    continue
+                if member.size < 0 or member.size > MAX_SOURCE_BYTES - expanded:
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream archive exceeds the expanded size limit.')
+                expanded += member.size
+                with source.extractfile(member) as stream:
+                    content = stream.read(member.size + 1)
+                if len(content) != member.size:
+                    raise ValueError('Upstream source member is truncated.')
+                files[name] = content
+    except (tarfile.TarError, EOFError, OSError) as error:
+        raise ValueError('Upstream source is not a complete gzip tar archive.') from error
+    for name in seen:
+        if any(parent.as_posix() in files for parent in PurePosixPath(name).parents):
+            raise ValueError('Upstream archive uses a file as a directory.')
+    plugin = lock['root'] + '/' + lock['plugin'] + '/'
+    if not any(name.startswith(plugin) for name in files):
+        raise ValueError('Upstream archive has no files in the pinned plugin subtree.')
+    return {name[len(lock['root']) + 1:]: content for name, content in files.items()}
+
+
+def main():
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
+    parser.add_argument('--archive', type=Path, required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--lock', type=Path, required=True)
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+    lock = load_lock(args.lock)
+    files = read_source(args.archive, lock)
+    print(json.dumps({'archive_sha256': lock['sha256'], 'commit': lock['commit'],
+                      'files': {name: hashlib.sha256(content).hexdigest()
+                                for name, content in sorted(files.items())}}, sort_keys=True))
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    main()
